 - 2026-06-17: PHASE A1 (HEADLINE; HARDEN the CLOSED in-generation moat) -- REPLICATE exp4315's reward-guided step-stitching win on a 2ND oracle-distinct corpus + MORE power. .399 (exp4315) CLOSED the in-generation moat oracle-distinctly: reward-guided step-stitching (2602.22871) with the leak-rechecked exp4292 partial-state scorer beat the best engaged control (EntRGi, +0.225) AND the model's INTRINSIC self-reward SMC (2602.01849, +0.35), guidance_moat_ci95 [0.075,0.375] EXCLUDING 0, controls_differentiated=true, scorer_leak_recheck_passed=true -- BUT on n=40/arm and a SINGLE multiple-choice reasoning corpus. The operator was TWICE-burned by premature DiffusionGemma over-claims (.396/.397), so before any DiffusionGemma-gate-flip claim the win MUST replicate on a DIFFERENT oracle-distinct reasoning corpus at MORE power (n>=80/arm, >=3 seeds). Reuse the EXACT exp4315 harness: unguided + the engaged control (EntRGi 2602.05000) + self-reward SMC (2602.01849, intrinsic, the must-beat baseline) + Carnot reward-guided stitching; the no-op guard (controls_differentiated); an INDEPENDENT leak re-check on the exp4292 scorer on THIS corpus. Emit in_generation_moat_replicates BARE bool := (Carnot-stitched - best-engaged-control > 0 AND CI95-excl-0 AND controls_differentiated AND Carnot-stitched - self-reward-SMC > 0) ON THE 2ND CORPUS. verifier_is_oracle=false. A replication is the strongest evidence yet (gate-flip candidate); a powered failure-to-replicate is decision-grade (the win was corpus-specific). NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission; DiffusionGemma via the llama.cpp PR binary. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=scorer_leaky_on_second_corpus; results/experiment_4325_in_generation_moat_replicate_second_corpus.json
 - 2026-06-17: PHASE A2 (HEADLINE; SCALE the CLOSED in-generation moat) -- ADAPTIVE guided-generation scale-up of the exp4315 win. .399 stitched the highest-scoring of DIVERSE complete trajectories; .400 scales to an ADAPTIVE generation loop where the leak-checked exp4292 partial-state scorer is the EXTERNAL reward that shapes DiffusionGemma's bounded adaptive denoising (insertion/unmasking schedule), per the .399 SOTA-ingestion flag. METHODS (VERIFY the exact arXiv ID in PRECONDITIONS before citing; if 2606.13565 cannot be verified, SUBSTITUTE the WebSearch-verified 2606.08501 reward-state alignment or 2603.12554 entropy-guided step selection): A2D2 adaptive any-length discrete diffusion (cited 2606.13565), TR2-D2 tree-search trajectory replay (2509.25171), Back-on-Track reward-state alignment (2606.08501). HARNESS (skeptic-proof, reuse exp4315/exp4308): a NO-ADAPTATION control + >=1 genuinely-engaged non-Carnot control + the no-op guard (controls_differentiated) + an INDEPENDENT leak re-check + frozen held-out. ASPIRATION (unify the headline with the north star): run the adaptive guidance on ARC-GRID generation (DiffusionGemma generates candidate ARC grids on the 256-mask canvas, the Carnot scorer rewards) -- if ARC-grid generation is infeasible in the window, fall back to a reasoning corpus and SAY SO. Emit adaptive_guidance_beats_control BARE bool := (Carnot-adaptive - best-engaged/no-adaptation control > 0 AND CI95-excl-0 AND controls_differentiated). verifier_is_oracle=false. NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission; DiffusionGemma via the llama.cpp PR binary. RE-SCOPE to fit the window (an honest partial reasoning-corpus run is COMPLETE). (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: adaptive_guidance_bounded_to_stitching_null; results/experiment_4326_adaptive_guided_generation_scaleup.json
 - 2026-06-17: PHASE B1 (ARC NORTH STAR; operator MANDATORY 2026-06-17) -- E3 EXECUTABLE-WORLD-MODEL solve of ar25 -> L1. The SOTA for FULL ARC-AGI-3 solves is the executable-world-model coding agent (arXiv:2605.05138: gpt-5.5 induces a Python world model, VERIFIES it reproduces observed transitions, refactors toward simpler abstractions, plans to the win; SOLVED 15/25 games, RHAE 58.12%). The harness is BUILT + validated end-to-end on ar25 (the codex agent induced a GENUINE flood-fill world model, the Carnot WorldModelVerifier grounded it at 61% vs 35% identity baseline); the only gap to a solve was the MULTI-ROUND refactor loop + win-seeking exploration. The codex agent IS the proposer (uses collect_transitions/WorldModelVerifier/load_engine/plan_and_execute as tools; WRITES results/arc_e3/ar25/world_model.py; do NOT nest a CodexProposer subprocess). INCREMENTAL-PROGRESS scoped: target +1 level (L1), NOT a full solve. HARD gate: offline_reproduced=true AND reproduced_levels>=1 (arc_solver_kit.reproduce) -- the real env reaching L1 via the induced-model plan, re-gated. An honest partial (best verifier_accuracy + the residual mismatch CLASS as a missing-world-model-rule gap) is PROGRESS. verifier_is_oracle=true (the SOLVE is EXECUTION-GROUNDED -- the real env defines the win -- ARC north-star progress, NOT an oracle-distinct moat headline). NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission; cap per-task wall-time to fit the window. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete_e3_ar25_partial_model_0.89; results/experiment_4327_e3_executable_world_model_ar25.json
